From 7cef23414399a02e62be8e836bf071c92b7dca66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jupiter Belic <belikh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:21:23 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] irix7: run the native PAL on the v0 syscall gate

Replace the provisional 0xffffffff-on-failure backend with the native
gate (syscall 0x1F7, CELL_E_* status in $2, value in $3) and map the
status through the shared status table to Err(Errno(...)).

Use relibc's 136-byte n32 struct stat directly.  The kernel now writes
that layout, so delete KernelStat and copy_stat.

Set $28 in _start to a 16-byte main-thread TCB (self at 0, dtv at 4,
errno at 8, libc-private at 12) and make errno read and write TP+8.
MIPS III has no rdhwr, so replace every #[thread_local] in the library
with a plain static on this target; SingleThread states the
single-threaded invariant at the declaration.

Read the auxiliary vector from $a3, store it for Stack::auxv, and use
the native auxv numbering so getauxval reports the kernel's values.
Keep getdents synthesised over the one-entry readdir call because the
kernel has no directory cookie.

Make futex wait/wake no-ops: the kernel has no futex and there is one
thread, so an ENOSYS there turns every mutex unlock into a panic.

Build with -mno-abicalls -G0; the std shim remains the exception.

Signed-off-by: Jupiter Belic <belikh@users.noreply.github.com>
